  * ` flags ` is ` undefined ` . 

In all other cases, calling ` RegExp() ` with or without ` new ` both create a
new ` RegExp ` object. If ` pattern ` is a regex, the new object's [ source
](/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/RegExp/source) is `
pattern.source ` ; otherwise, its source is ` pattern ` [ coerced to a string
](/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/String#string_coercion)
. If the ` flags ` parameter is not ` undefined ` , the new object's [ ` flags
` ](/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/RegExp/flags) is the
parameter's value; otherwise, its ` flags ` is ` pattern.flags ` (if ` pattern
` is a regex).
